 Shapiro ahead by roughly 20 to 30 points, every major rater calls the race Safe or Solid Democratic, and markets price near certainty, so the fundamentals-only estimate of a smaller edge is outweighed by this consistent evidence.", "watch": "Only an unforeseen late scandal or dramatic national event would meaningfully narrow a lead this large.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's governor's race pits incumbent Democrat Josh Shapiro against Republican Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Polling since summer has shown Shapiro ahead by 19 to 30 points, with likely-voter surveys from Quinnipiac and Siena placing the margin near 20 to 25 points. The average of recent polls sits around 24 points, and even Republican-leaning pollsters show a double-digit race.\n\nEvery major rating outlet, including Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, and Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets give Shapiro roughly 97 percent odds. Garrity has campaigned on affordability and tariffs and shared a debate stage with Shapiro, but has not closed the gap. The state's slight Republican lean is outweighed by Shapiro's incumbency and broad standing. A major external shock is the main path to a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.0